  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.2.1: Dependency refresh, patch release because no public API changed and no Redis code changed. This build declares CoreSystem.Cache.Rehydration 2.2.1 and CoreSystem.Cache 3.1.2, so the pin moves announced in 2.2.0 are now in effect. Through CoreSystem.Cache 3.1.2 it resolves CoreSystem.Memory 1.1.1, CoreSystem.Resilience 2.1.1 and CoreSystem.Serialization 1.3.1, which are the versions this package is built and tested against, so consumers stop pulling the older 1.1.0, 2.1.0 and 1.3.0 graph. The packed README was refreshed since 2.2.0. AddCoreCacheRedis behaves exactly as in 2.2.0, and the AddHealthChecks() prerequisite still applies: without it the redis_cache health check is never registered and rehydration cannot observe a recovery.",
